@page "/creator-agreement"
@inherits CreatorAgreementModel

<PageTitle>Creator Agreement - Streamtunes</PageTitle>

<div class="container my-5">
    <h1 class="mb-4">Creator Agreement</h1>
    
    <p class="text-muted"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> January 8, 2026</p>

    <div class="terms-content">
        <p>
            This Creator Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into between Streamtunes ("Platform," "we," "us," or "our") 
            and the individual or entity registering as a creator ("Creator," "you," or "your").
        </p>
        <p>
            By uploading content or receiving payouts through the Platform, you agree to the terms below.
        </p>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>1. Platform Description</h2>
            <p>
                The Platform is a subscription-based music streaming service. Users pay the Platform for access to stream music. 
                Creators are compensated via royalty payouts based on streaming activity.
            </p>
            <p>
                Creators are not sellers, not merchants of record, and do not transact directly with end users.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>2. Eligibility and Account Setup</h2>
            <p>To participate as a Creator, you must:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Be at least 18 years old</li>
                <li>Complete payout onboarding through our designated payment provider</li>
                <li>Complete tax form onboarding through our designated tax accounting service</li>
                <li>Provide accurate tax and identity information</li>
                <li>Maintain an active payout-enabled account</li>
            </ul>
            
            <h3>2.1 Tax Form Onboarding</h3>
            <p>
                As part of the creator onboarding process, you will be required to complete tax form onboarding 
                through our designated tax accounting service. This process includes:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Receiving an email from our Platform notifying you of the tax form requirement</li>
                <li>Receiving a separate email from our tax accounting service provider with a secure link</li>
                <li>Completing the appropriate tax form (W-9 for U.S. persons or W-8 for non-U.S. persons)</li>
                <li>Submitting accurate and complete tax information</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                You must complete the appropriate tax form before you can be fully onboarded as a Creator and 
                begin receiving royalty payouts.
            </p>
            <p>
                Failure to complete onboarding may result in delayed or withheld payouts.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>3. Ownership and License Grant</h2>
            <p>You represent and warrant that:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>You own or control all necessary rights to the content you upload</li>
                <li>Your content does not infringe any third-party rights</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                You retain full ownership of your content.
            </p>
            <p>
                You grant the Platform a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Host</li>
                <li>Stream</li>
                <li>Cache</li>
                <li>Display</li>
                <li>Transmit</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                your content solely for the operation and promotion of the Platform.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>4. Royalties and Payouts</h2>
            
            <h3>4.1 Royalty Calculation</h3>
            <p>
                Royalties are calculated based on qualifying streams, defined as continuous playback of at least 30 seconds.
            </p>
            <p>
                The current royalty rate is published on the Platform and may be updated at our discretion.
            </p>

            <h3>4.2 Payment Timing</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Royalties are accrued internally</li>
                <li>Payouts are issued on a weekly basis</li>
                <li>Minimum payout thresholds may apply</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>5. Taxes</h2>
            <p>
                Creators are independent contractors.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>The Platform does not withhold taxes</li>
                <li>You are responsible for reporting income</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>5.1 Tax Forms</h3>
            <p>
                As part of the creator onboarding process, you are required to complete the appropriate tax form 
                through our designated tax accounting service:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>U.S. Persons:</strong> You will complete IRS Form W-9 (Request for Taxpayer Identification Number and Certification)</li>
                <li><strong>Non-U.S. Persons:</strong> You will complete the appropriate IRS Form W-8 (such as W-8BEN or W-8BEN-E)</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Your tax information is securely collected and stored by our designated tax accounting service provider.
            </p>

            <h3>5.2 Tax Reporting</h3>
            <p>
                Based on your tax status and earnings, you may receive the following tax documents:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Form 1099-NEC or 1099-MISC:</strong> Issued to U.S. persons who meet IRS reporting thresholds</li>
                <li><strong>Form 1042-S:</strong> Issued to non-U.S. persons for reporting income subject to withholding</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Tax forms will be issued in accordance with applicable IRS requirements and deadlines.
            </p>
            <p>
                The Platform may suspend payouts if required tax information is not provided.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>6. Content Standards and Enforcement</h2>
            <p>You agree not to upload content that:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Infringes copyrights or trademarks</li>
                <li>Is unlawful, deceptive, or fraudulent</li>
                <li>Contains malware or malicious code</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We reserve the right to remove content or suspend accounts at our sole discretion.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>7. DMCA Compliance Policy</h2>
            <p>
                The Platform complies with the Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA).
            </p>

            <h3>7.1 Copyright Complaints</h3>
            <p>If you believe content infringes your copyright, send a written notice including:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Your contact information</li>
                <li>Identification of the copyrighted work</li>
                <li>Identification of the infringing content</li>
                <li>A statement of good-faith belief</li>
                <li>A statement under penalty of perjury</li>
                <li>Your physical or electronic signature</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Send notices to:
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>DMCA Agent:</strong><br />
                Email: <a href="mailto:customerservice@streamtunes.net">customerservice@streamtunes.net</a>
            </p>

            <h3>7.2 Counter-Notification</h3>
            <p>
                If your content is removed due to a DMCA notice, you may submit a counter-notification as permitted by law.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>8. Refund Policy</h2>
            <p>
                The Platform does not offer refunds for subscription payments.
            </p>
            <p>
                Royalty payouts to Creators are final once issued.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>9. Suspension and Termination</h2>
            <p>We may suspend or terminate your account if:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>You violate this Agreement</li>
                <li>You fail identity or tax verification</li>
                <li>Your content creates legal or compliance risk</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Upon termination:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Outstanding accrued royalties may be paid</li>
                <li>Content licenses terminate</li>
                <li>Access is revoked</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>10. Limitation of Liability</h2>
            <p>
                To the maximum extent permitted by law:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>The Platform is not liable for lost profits</li>
                <li>Liability is limited to royalties paid in the preceding 12 months</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>11. Indemnification</h2>
            <p>You agree to indemnify and hold harmless the Platform from claims arising from:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Uploaded content</li>
                <li>Breach of this Agreement</li>
                <li>Intellectual property violations</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>12. Governing Law</h2>
            <p>
                This Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Nevada, without regard to conflict-of-law principles.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>13. Privacy Note (Creator-Specific)</h2>
            <p>
                Creator payout and tax information is handled securely by our payment processor. 
                The Platform does not store full tax identification numbers.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2>14. Changes</h2>
            <p>
                We may update this Agreement. Continued participation constitutes acceptance of changes.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>
